{number: 124}
{title: The First Noel}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
The [C] first No-[G] el the [F] angel did [C] say
Was to [F] certain poor [C] shepherds in [F] fields as they [C] lay;
In [C] fields where [G] they lay [F] keeping their [C] sheep,
On a [F] cold winter's [C] night that [F] was so [C] deep.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
No-[C] el, No-[Em] el, No-[F] el, No-[C] el,
[F] Born is the [C] King of [F] Is-[G7] ra-[C] el.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
They [C] looked [G] up and [F] saw a [C] star
Shining [F] in the [C] east, be-[F] yond them [C] far;
And [C] to the [G] earth it [F] gave great [C] light,
And [F] so it con-[C] tinued both [F] day and [C] night.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
And [C] by the [G] light of [F] that same [C] star
Three [F] Wise Men [C] came from [F] country [C] far;
To [C] seek for a [G] king was [F] their in-[C] tent,
And to [F] follow the [C] star wher-[F] ever it [C] went.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Then [C] let us [G] all with [F] one ac-[C] cord
Sing [F] praises [C] to our [F] heav'nly [C] Lord;
That [C] hath made [G] heav'n and [F] earth of [C] naught,
And [F] with His [C] blood man-[F] kind hath [C] bought.
{end_of_verse}
